      "hunks": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "end": 11,
          "lines": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "# H16 v2 image serving candidate"
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "Implemented experimental source; CPU contract tests use a fake engine and provide no model-quality or GPU qualification. The real v1 backend remains unavailable and v1 mock metadata remains strict. Production readiness is never enabled by the candidate path or caller flags."
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "`POST /v2/hala/action` accepts exactly `schema: hala.image_request.v2`, `policy_request` (the existing strict v1 request used only as a pure policy record), and `media`. Media requires bounded PNG base64, SHA-256, request/tenant/task/device/session IDs, `frame_id` equal to observation generation, `origin: [0,0]`, and `dpi: 96`. Only identity image scaling is supported; dimensions must match the PNG, and images are limited to 524288 bytes and 1048576 pixels. Existing transport body limits may impose a smaller bound; raising them is explicit server configuration. Redaction regions must contain black pixels. Media digests bind bytes to the submitted observation, not to a trusted capture device; future Aladdin integration must supply authenticated fresh observations."
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "The engine receives one RGB image and the goal; the remote prompt does not include observed IDs or private bounds. The independent v2 protocol `h16-v2-normalized-point-v1` accepts only `{\"point\":[x,y]}` with integer axes in 0..1000, either bare JSON or exactly one `json` code fence. No prose extraction, duplicate fields, extra fields or guessed protocol are accepted. The server maps each coordinate by `min(size-1, coordinate*size//1000)`, identifies exactly one eligible observed target, rejects protected or ambiguous overlapping hits, and reuses deterministic action policy validation. Confidence is `null`: model confidence is uncalibrated and is not requested or invented. Output `hala.click_proposal.v2` carries all bindings, media digest and engine/model/processor/prompt/precision provenance. It is unqualified advice with `execution_authorized: false` and `verification_required: true`; it contains no success receipt. `/v2/hala/plan` and `/v2/hala/decision` fail closed. Authentication, admission leases, framing, deadline, disconnect cancellation and output limits reuse the existing transport. `/ready` remains the existing v1 backend readiness and does not claim v2 qualification."
            },
            {
              "n": 8,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 9,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "`CandidateBackend()` is unavailable by default. A server-owned injected engine enables experimental candidate calls only. CPU tests label provenance `cpu_fake`. `RemoteQwenEngine.load(cache_dir)` is an optional remote-only Linux Colab loader requiring explicit `HALA_REMOTE_SERVING_ALLOWED=1` and an actual `COLAB_RELEASE_TAG` marker. It rejects the Kaggle runtime marker and an unknown `/kaggle` runtime, local Windows, and caches outside `/content` or the approved `/tmp/hala-serving-model-cache` before importing ML packages. Kaggle commercial-use eligibility remains blocked. Provider markers are diagnostics, not an adversarial proof or permission to spend. It pins Qwen/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct revision `89644892e4d85e24eaac8bacfd4f463576704203`, Torch 2.11.0 and Transformers 5.16.1, FP16, eager attention and `trust_remote_code=False`. It uses a 4096-token input ceiling, deterministic bounded 96-token generation and context stopping, with one active shared model call. Deadline cannot preempt an in-progress CUDA kernel; admission stays retained until the worker finishes."
            },
            {
              "n": 10,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "n": 11,
              "sign": "+",
              "text": "No loader execution, downloaded weights, GPU E2E, release qualification, native Aladdin integration, training, public tunnel or deployment is included in CPU evidence. Actual free-session GPU serving evidence and independent Jev/PStack/Graft/CI gates remain required. Do not install these ML packages or call the loader on the personal PC."
            }
          ],
          "dropped": 0
        }
      ]
